WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.714 --> 00:00:03.007
[horn sounding]

00:00:05.218 --> 00:00:07.637
[horns sounding]

00:00:07.637 --> 00:00:10.098
Caroline Aghajanian: On the season
finale of "Travel Dares,"

00:00:10.098 --> 00:00:13.643
Nico Reyes: I'm taking Caroline to learn
how to play the Swiss alphorn.

00:00:13.643 --> 00:00:14.561
[horn sounding]

00:00:14.561 --> 00:00:15.520
Aj Caldwell: And I'm taking Caroline

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.814
to learn how to make Swiss cowbells.

00:00:17.814 --> 00:00:19.941
[bell ringing]

00:00:19.941 --> 00:00:21.609
Caroline: Come
join us on our adventures

00:00:21.609 --> 00:00:24.237
on this episode of "Travel Dares."

00:00:29.325 --> 00:00:30.618
Caroline: This is "Travel Dares,"

00:00:30.618 --> 00:00:33.538
the show where we do daring
activities all over Europe

00:00:33.538 --> 00:00:36.374
empowered by my Marriott
Bonvoy Boundless card.

00:00:36.374 --> 00:00:38.710
We've been to seven amazing cities so far,

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:41.713
and we're ending our journey
in Lucerne, Switzerland.

00:00:41.713 --> 00:00:44.048
Aj: To thank you for
taking us all over Europe,

00:00:44.048 --> 00:00:47.010
me and Nico are taking
you on two special dares.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.512
Caroline: Yes! That's a lot
of time in the blindfold,

00:00:49.512 --> 00:00:50.764
but I'm super excited.

00:00:50.764 --> 00:00:53.141
Nico: We're gonna start
off with my dare first,

00:00:53.141 --> 00:00:54.309
the better dare.

00:00:54.309 --> 00:00:55.602
Here's your clue.

00:00:55.602 --> 00:00:56.895
Caroline: Did you hear
that? The better dare.

00:00:56.895 --> 00:00:59.230
Aj: Yeah, we're saving the
best for last, it's fine.

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:02.817
Caroline: We're going back to school!

00:01:02.817 --> 00:01:05.069
We were just in Cambridge, Nico.

00:01:05.069 --> 00:01:07.447
Nico: Listen, we all know
that these clues mean nothing.

00:01:07.447 --> 00:01:09.407
[all laughing]

00:01:09.407 --> 00:01:11.910
Caroline: My first instinct
is to think of, like, a book.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:15.872
A textbook? But no, it has
something to do with music notes.

00:01:15.872 --> 00:01:17.415
Music notes!

00:01:17.415 --> 00:01:18.666
I'm nervous!

00:01:18.666 --> 00:01:19.959
Nico: Towards this way.
Aj: All right,

00:01:19.959 --> 00:01:21.377
we're gonna go this way, into the grass.

00:01:21.377 --> 00:01:22.337
Caroline: Oh, God.

00:01:22.337 --> 00:01:23.755
Nico: Now it's a little bit easier.

00:01:23.755 --> 00:01:25.089
Caroline: It's very uneven.

00:01:25.089 --> 00:01:26.716
You guys, I'm really overwhelmed.

00:01:26.716 --> 00:01:27.884
Do I take off my blindfold?

00:01:27.884 --> 00:01:28.718
Nico: No! Not yet!

00:01:28.718 --> 00:01:30.220
Caroline: Oh, my God, OK.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:32.263
[horn sounds]
[Caroline screams]

00:01:32.263 --> 00:01:33.973
Oh, my God, oh, my God!

00:01:33.973 --> 00:01:36.768
[all laughing]

00:01:36.768 --> 00:01:39.354
Nico: Today we're gonna learn
how to play the Swiss alphorn.

00:01:39.354 --> 00:01:42.565
Caroline: Oh, my God.

00:01:42.565 --> 00:01:43.817
Nico: Look at this thing.

00:01:43.817 --> 00:01:45.819
Caroline: That's such a long horn!

00:01:52.867 --> 00:01:54.702
Caroline: Got it!
Nico: All right, let's go.

00:01:54.702 --> 00:01:55.537
Caroline: I feel like this is something

00:01:55.537 --> 00:01:56.746
you only see in movies.

00:01:56.746 --> 00:01:57.580
Aj: I know!

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:58.832
Caroline: All right,
now, how do we do this?

00:01:58.832 --> 00:02:01.292
Nico: OK, guys. There are
three things that we gotta do.

00:02:01.292 --> 00:02:03.628
First, we gotta figure out
how to play this thing.

00:02:03.628 --> 00:02:06.631
Second, we're gonna figure
out how to hold these notes,

00:02:06.631 --> 00:02:08.508
and third is that we're gonna figure out

00:02:08.508 --> 00:02:10.134
how we can play all together

00:02:10.134 --> 00:02:12.095
like a little Swiss alphorn band.

00:02:12.095 --> 00:02:13.263
Think you guys can handle all that?

00:02:13.263 --> 00:02:14.430
Aj: Oh, I can handle it.
Caroline: Yeah, definitely.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:16.015
Nico: I'm talking as if
I've played this thing

00:02:16.015 --> 00:02:17.767
my whole life.

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:19.477
Anique: Hi, guys, my name is Anique,

00:02:19.477 --> 00:02:21.521
and I'm the translator of Willi.

00:02:21.521 --> 00:02:23.273
He plays the alphorn professional,

00:02:23.273 --> 00:02:26.484
and he's gonna show you guys
how to play the alphorn.

00:02:26.484 --> 00:02:29.070
[horn sounds]

00:02:38.413 --> 00:02:39.789
Nico: I love this song.

00:02:39.789 --> 00:02:40.957
Caroline: There's so many notes.

00:02:40.957 --> 00:02:42.000
Aj: I know!

00:02:42.876 --> 00:02:43.835
Caroline: Good job, Willi.

00:02:45.086 --> 00:02:46.296
[mouthpiece toots]

00:02:46.296 --> 00:02:47.422
[horn toots]

00:02:47.422 --> 00:02:49.632
Nico: Wow! You did it, Aj!

00:02:49.632 --> 00:02:50.717
Aj: I got it!

00:02:52.051 --> 00:02:54.971
Nico: Everyone gets a
hat when they do good.

00:02:54.971 --> 00:02:56.222
Oh, my God!

00:02:56.222 --> 00:02:57.307
Willi: Very good.

00:02:57.307 --> 00:02:59.851
[horn squeaks]
[Nico laughs]

00:02:59.851 --> 00:03:01.644
Nico: Hoo!
[all laughing]

00:03:01.644 --> 00:03:04.439
That was me, it wasn't the horn.

00:03:04.439 --> 00:03:05.648
[horn sounding]

00:03:05.648 --> 00:03:07.775
[all cheering]

00:03:07.775 --> 00:03:08.860
[mouthpiece toots]

00:03:10.111 --> 00:03:11.487
[laughs]

00:03:12.739 --> 00:03:13.573
[horn sounding]

00:03:13.573 --> 00:03:15.825
Nico: Yay!
Aj: Yes! That's so good!

00:03:15.825 --> 00:03:17.118
Caroline: I literally have to, like,

00:03:17.118 --> 00:03:18.786
[blows raspberries] in there.

00:03:18.786 --> 00:03:20.955
[horns sound]

00:03:25.376 --> 00:03:26.294
[squeals]

00:03:26.294 --> 00:03:27.253
Nico: That sounded pretty good.

00:03:27.253 --> 00:03:28.254
Caroline: That was amazing!

00:03:28.254 --> 00:03:30.465
Nico: OK, so we know how to play them now.

00:03:30.465 --> 00:03:34.385
Now we just have to figure
out how to hold a tone.

00:03:34.385 --> 00:03:35.970
OK, so here's a little challenge.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.848
Let's try to do low, medium, high notes.

00:03:38.848 --> 00:03:39.807
Aj, you start.

00:03:39.807 --> 00:03:40.808
Aj: All right.

00:03:40.808 --> 00:03:42.769
[clears throat]
[exhales]

00:03:42.769 --> 00:03:44.646
Aj: Here we go.

00:03:44.646 --> 00:03:48.232
[horn sounding weakly]

00:03:48.232 --> 00:03:49.108
I forgot how to do this!

00:03:49.108 --> 00:03:50.652
Nico: Are you sure you played the trumpet?

00:03:50.652 --> 00:03:51.736
Were you lying?
Aj: No, I did not play the

00:03:51.736 --> 00:03:54.906
trumpet, I played the saxophone.

00:03:54.906 --> 00:03:57.367
[horn sounding]

00:03:57.367 --> 00:03:58.451
Aj: Wasn't fair!

00:03:58.451 --> 00:03:59.953
Caroline: That was great!

00:03:59.953 --> 00:04:01.746
Nico: I still sound a little busted, but.

00:04:01.746 --> 00:04:02.997
Caroline: That was good.

00:04:02.997 --> 00:04:05.124
[horn trumpeting]
[laughing]

00:04:07.001 --> 00:04:08.419
Can I redo the high one?

00:04:08.419 --> 00:04:09.712
Aj: I don't understand!

00:04:09.712 --> 00:04:11.047
[playing up the scale]

00:04:11.047 --> 00:04:12.632
Nico: Smooth!
Aj: That's smooth!

00:04:13.466 --> 00:04:15.718
Nico! Yes!
Aj: Whoa!

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:18.638
Caroline: I'ma pass out.

00:04:18.638 --> 00:04:19.472
Aj: That's it!

00:04:19.472 --> 00:04:21.057
Nico: It's time for our
big band performance.

00:04:21.057 --> 00:04:22.141
I'm really nervous.

00:04:22.141 --> 00:04:23.559
Caroline: Yeah, it's the moment of truth.

00:04:23.559 --> 00:04:24.727
Nico: It's the moment of truth, let's see

00:04:24.727 --> 00:04:27.313
if we retained any knowledge today.

00:04:27.313 --> 00:04:28.982
OK. All right.
Caroline: Let's do it.

00:04:28.982 --> 00:04:30.984
Nico: Let's break it down.

00:04:30.984 --> 00:04:34.737
[horns hooting rhythmically]

00:04:37.365 --> 00:04:40.159
[horns bellowing]

00:04:43.538 --> 00:04:45.790
[cheering]
[laughing]

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:46.874
Caroline: That was really good.

00:04:46.874 --> 00:04:47.917
Nico: Amazing. Thank you.

00:04:47.917 --> 00:04:49.961
Thank you, thank you,
sheep, thank you, goats.

00:04:49.961 --> 00:04:51.963
Caroline: I am, like,
really peaceful right now,

00:04:51.963 --> 00:04:53.715
so just leave me here.

00:04:53.715 --> 00:04:55.383
Did you guys hear that?

00:04:55.383 --> 00:04:56.384
Encore?

00:04:56.384 --> 00:04:58.177
All: Encore! Encore!

00:04:58.177 --> 00:04:59.971
Encore! Here we go!

00:04:59.971 --> 00:05:02.807
[horns bellowing]

00:05:06.602 --> 00:05:08.855
Aj: All right, Caroline, I
know you had a good time,

00:05:08.855 --> 00:05:10.732
but are you ready to
have an even better time

00:05:10.732 --> 00:05:13.317
with my day?
Caroline: Yes! Ooh.

00:05:16.863 --> 00:05:19.615
OK, are we, like, redoing
a dare or something?

00:05:19.615 --> 00:05:20.658
Aj: I don't know.

00:05:20.658 --> 00:05:21.576
Nico: Think about it.

00:05:21.576 --> 00:05:22.952
Caroline: I'm, like, thinking
over all of the dares.

00:05:22.952 --> 00:05:24.162
We've done a lot of dares.

00:05:24.162 --> 00:05:25.538
Nico: We've done a lot of dares.

00:05:25.538 --> 00:05:27.123
Caroline: I feel like
we're gonna be doing a dare

00:05:27.123 --> 00:05:28.374
that we've already done but, like,

00:05:28.374 --> 00:05:30.293
amp it up, like, times 100.

00:05:30.293 --> 00:05:31.919
Aj: Slide over.

00:05:31.919 --> 00:05:33.212
Nico: Right here.

00:05:33.212 --> 00:05:34.964
Caroline: OK, all right.
Aj: Are you ready, Caroline?

00:05:34.964 --> 00:05:36.049
Caroline: Yep.

00:05:36.049 --> 00:05:37.592
[bell ringing]
[screams]

00:05:37.592 --> 00:05:39.135
[laughing]
Caroline: What is this?

00:05:39.135 --> 00:05:40.762
Aj: Today we're learning
how to make cowbells!

00:05:40.762 --> 00:05:42.513
Caroline: Oh, my God, wow!

00:05:42.513 --> 00:05:43.723
Wait, that thing is huge!

00:05:43.723 --> 00:05:45.391
Can I try?
Aj: Yeah.

00:05:45.391 --> 00:05:46.434
[bell ringing]

00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:47.894
Caroline: Oh, my God, it's heavy.

00:05:56.778 --> 00:05:57.779
Caroline: Nice to meet you.

00:05:57.779 --> 00:05:59.197
Olivia Rast: Nice to meet you, I'm Olivia.

00:05:59.197 --> 00:06:00.907
Caroline: Olivia, so nice to meet you.

00:06:00.907 --> 00:06:02.658
What is the first step?

00:06:02.658 --> 00:06:05.995
Olivia: So, first, they have
to fill this form with sand.

00:06:05.995 --> 00:06:08.664
Caroline: So, this. Ooh, this is heavy.

00:06:08.664 --> 00:06:10.124
And right here.

00:06:10.958 --> 00:06:12.043
Ooh, that feels good.

00:06:12.043 --> 00:06:14.545
It's a nice chunk of cold sand.

00:06:14.545 --> 00:06:16.297
More sand. Well, all right.

00:06:17.465 --> 00:06:19.008
Oh!

00:06:19.008 --> 00:06:20.510
[machine whirring]
[Caroline screams]

00:06:23.221 --> 00:06:25.098
Nico: I feel like these
steps are a little scary,

00:06:25.098 --> 00:06:27.642
but she's confidently doing them.

00:06:29.227 --> 00:06:31.062
Caroline: Who would have known I had

00:06:31.062 --> 00:06:32.647
these bell-making skills?

00:06:32.647 --> 00:06:34.107
Aj knew, for sure.

00:06:34.107 --> 00:06:35.233
Olivia: These are the forms.

00:06:35.233 --> 00:06:36.734
Nico: Oh, they're flowers.

00:06:36.734 --> 00:06:37.777
Olivia: To put on the stamps.

00:06:37.777 --> 00:06:39.654
So, they have all the letters,

00:06:39.654 --> 00:06:42.198
so, if you, as a customer you have a wish,

00:06:42.198 --> 00:06:45.076
they can write everything
you want into the bell.

00:06:45.076 --> 00:06:46.369
Caroline: One, two, and.

00:06:48.871 --> 00:06:52.041
Yeah! We finally got it.

00:06:54.836 --> 00:06:55.670
Nico: OK.

00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:56.504
Caroline: Come take a
look at my masterpiece.

00:06:56.504 --> 00:06:57.588
Nico: Let's inspect it.

00:06:57.588 --> 00:06:58.422
Olivia: Wow.
Aj: Hmm.

00:06:58.422 --> 00:06:59.590
Nico: I don't even know
what I'm looking for,

00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:01.384
but it looks right.

00:07:01.384 --> 00:07:02.593
Caroline: Ah!

00:07:02.593 --> 00:07:03.803
Aj: Whoa!

00:07:03.803 --> 00:07:05.555
Caroline: Look, they're
about to make my bell!

00:07:05.555 --> 00:07:06.848
Nico: Oh, my God.

00:07:06.848 --> 00:07:08.516
Caroline: Yay!
Nico: Whoa!

00:07:08.516 --> 00:07:11.644
Olivia: At this place, they
are making the very special,

00:07:11.644 --> 00:07:13.855
valuable cowbells.

00:07:13.855 --> 00:07:18.067
In Switzerland, we make,
like, presents for weddings

00:07:18.067 --> 00:07:21.195
or birthdays or special events.

00:07:21.195 --> 00:07:25.741
And here you can see how this
family creates the bells.

00:07:25.741 --> 00:07:27.702
It's a family tradition,

00:07:27.702 --> 00:07:31.164
and you can make your own cowbells

00:07:31.164 --> 00:07:35.501
with customized design with letters.

00:07:42.175 --> 00:07:44.677
Caroline: Oh, I know
my bell when I see her.

00:07:44.677 --> 00:07:45.928
There she is!

00:07:45.928 --> 00:07:50.183
Ooh, this is my bell!
And she's a heavy one.

00:07:50.183 --> 00:07:52.435
Come on! Whoo!

00:07:52.435 --> 00:07:53.561
She's beautiful.

00:07:53.561 --> 00:07:55.688
Next step, polishing station.

00:07:55.688 --> 00:07:57.773
I'm just gonna brush the bell a little.

00:08:01.903 --> 00:08:05.489
Oh, my God, this is, like, real gold.

00:08:05.489 --> 00:08:07.575
It's looking really good.

00:08:07.575 --> 00:08:08.701
Look, guys!

00:08:08.701 --> 00:08:09.702
Look at it.

00:08:09.702 --> 00:08:10.661
How does it look?

00:08:10.661 --> 00:08:12.455
Nico: Wow, it's so shiny.
Aj: It looks good.

00:08:12.455 --> 00:08:13.372
Caroline: It's my little bell.

00:08:13.372 --> 00:08:14.916
Aj: The stamps you put
in came out really well.

00:08:14.916 --> 00:08:15.750
Nico: It looks great, it looks great.

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:16.584
Caroline: Thank you, thank you.

00:08:16.584 --> 00:08:19.045
Now it's the moment of
truth. How does it sound?

00:08:19.045 --> 00:08:20.630
Nico: OK, all right.

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:22.882
[bell ringing]

00:08:22.882 --> 00:08:23.925
Nico: It sounds like a bell.

00:08:23.925 --> 00:08:25.509
Aj: Sounds like a cowbell.

00:08:25.509 --> 00:08:26.677
Nico: A cowbell!

00:08:26.677 --> 00:08:28.971
Caroline: It's beautiful. I'm so proud.

00:08:28.971 --> 00:08:31.349
I got my bell, I got my belt.

00:08:31.349 --> 00:08:33.684
I don't know how I'm gonna
fit it into my luggage.

00:08:33.684 --> 00:08:34.769
Nico: It's gonna make it so heavy.

00:08:34.769 --> 00:08:36.395
Caroline: Perfect! Yay!

00:08:36.395 --> 00:08:38.105
Can you grab my bell?
Nico: Let's go.

00:08:38.105 --> 00:08:39.607
Caroline: I actually had so much fun

00:08:39.607 --> 00:08:41.108
on this dare. Thank you.

00:08:41.108 --> 00:08:41.943
Nico: Me too.

00:08:41.943 --> 00:08:42.860
Aj: I'm glad you guys enjoyed it,

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:45.529
but I do have one more surprise...

00:08:45.529 --> 00:08:46.697
a double dare.

00:08:46.697 --> 00:08:48.157
Nico: Another dare?
Caroline: What?

00:08:48.157 --> 00:08:49.450
Aj: Another dare for the both of you.

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:50.701
Nico: What, now?

00:08:50.701 --> 00:08:51.577
Aj: Blindfold up!

00:08:51.577 --> 00:08:53.329
Caroline: Wait, I'm
actually kind of excited.

00:08:53.329 --> 00:08:56.332
Nico: I'm nervous, I
was not in on this one.

00:08:56.332 --> 00:08:58.668
Aj: Here we go, I got
you. All right, you ready?

00:08:58.668 --> 00:08:59.877
Caroline: Oh, good. OK, this way.

00:08:59.877 --> 00:09:02.213
Caroline: Here's the thing,
you planned this surprise,

00:09:02.213 --> 00:09:03.881
you don't even give us a clue.

00:09:03.881 --> 00:09:05.758
Nico: We can't have a clue?

00:09:05.758 --> 00:09:06.592
Caroline: We don't have a clue.

00:09:06.592 --> 00:09:07.969
Aj: No clues, no clues.

00:09:07.969 --> 00:09:09.470
Nico: Oh, my God.
Caroline: Nothing at all.

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:10.638
Aj: Just gonna show up and enjoy.

00:09:10.638 --> 00:09:12.765
Caroline and Nico will never guess

00:09:12.765 --> 00:09:14.558
the surprise I have planned for them.

00:09:14.558 --> 00:09:18.646
Down the hill, a little slower,
Nico, Caroline's behind you.

00:09:18.646 --> 00:09:19.981
Nico: OK.

00:09:19.981 --> 00:09:20.815
Caroline: Oh, my God,
oh, my God, oh, my God.

00:09:20.815 --> 00:09:21.857
Aj: OK, perfect.

00:09:21.857 --> 00:09:22.692
Caroline: Oh, my God.

00:09:22.692 --> 00:09:23.776
Aj: Now take off your blindfolds,

00:09:23.776 --> 00:09:25.444
'cause we're meeting Swiss cows.

00:09:25.444 --> 00:09:28.364
[screaming]
[laughing]

00:09:28.364 --> 00:09:29.907
[bells jingling]

00:09:32.285 --> 00:09:34.787
Caroline: Oh, my God.

00:09:34.787 --> 00:09:36.664
Hi.
Nico: They're so big.

00:09:36.664 --> 00:09:39.458
Nico: I'm Nico. Oh, caress.

00:09:39.458 --> 00:09:41.294
Olivia: The cowbells are very important

00:09:41.294 --> 00:09:46.090
because usually the cows are
by themselves in the mountains

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:47.341
and so you can hear them.

00:09:47.341 --> 00:09:50.052
You can hear where your herd is,

00:09:50.052 --> 00:09:52.179
and you don't have to go and find them

00:09:52.179 --> 00:09:53.848
because you know where they are.

00:09:53.848 --> 00:09:56.517
Caroline: I've never touched a cow before.

00:09:56.517 --> 00:09:58.477
You're so cute.

00:09:58.477 --> 00:10:01.022
Aj, this is the best surprise ever.

00:10:01.022 --> 00:10:01.939
Oh, my God.

00:10:01.939 --> 00:10:02.857
Aj: I knew you guys would love it.

00:10:02.857 --> 00:10:03.691
Nico: This is super fun.

00:10:03.691 --> 00:10:07.445
I do love cows, cows
are my favorite animal.

00:10:07.445 --> 00:10:08.946
Caroline: Bye.

00:10:08.946 --> 00:10:12.616
Nico: Bye, ladies, it was a
pleasure meeting all of you.

00:10:12.616 --> 00:10:14.160
Caroline: You're so cute, bye-bye.

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:17.038
Aj: We've enjoyed our time here.

00:10:17.038 --> 00:10:18.205
Aj: Bye!

00:10:21.125 --> 00:10:23.502
Caroline: You guys, Switzerland
has been so amazing,

00:10:23.502 --> 00:10:25.796
so beautiful, people are so nice.

00:10:25.796 --> 00:10:29.717
Lucerne is such, like, a cute,
small, quaint little town.

00:10:29.717 --> 00:10:30.968
Kinda like this hotel.

00:10:30.968 --> 00:10:33.554
Aj: And look at this
spread. It looks so good.

00:10:33.554 --> 00:10:34.555
Nico: So good.

00:10:34.555 --> 00:10:35.848
Caroline: Starving.

00:10:35.848 --> 00:10:36.682
Nico: Me too.

00:10:36.682 --> 00:10:37.516
Caroline: Moment of truth.

00:10:37.516 --> 00:10:41.062
My final rating, and I
get two this time, so,

00:10:41.062 --> 00:10:43.731
Nico, you start, yeah.
Nico: I'll go first.

00:10:43.731 --> 00:10:45.274
I didn't know what to expect

00:10:45.274 --> 00:10:47.360
when you went up there
with that Swiss alphorn.

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:51.530
It is not an easy thing to
play, to pick up, to learn,

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:53.824
but you were so passionate and determined

00:10:53.824 --> 00:10:55.159
to learn all those tones,

00:10:55.159 --> 00:10:56.494
so I think I have to give you

00:10:56.494 --> 00:10:58.329
a five-star rating.
Caroline: Yes! Yes!

00:10:58.329 --> 00:11:00.414
Nico: You even impressed Willi,

00:11:00.414 --> 00:11:01.665
our teacher!
Caroline: Oh, my gosh.

00:11:02.625 --> 00:11:04.502
And Aj?

00:11:04.502 --> 00:11:07.755
Aj: All right, so, Caroline,
for the cowbell making,

00:11:07.755 --> 00:11:09.882
you were so excited to do it.

00:11:09.882 --> 00:11:13.219
You were super involved at
every step of the process,

00:11:13.219 --> 00:11:16.013
and I'm really proud of the
way that your bell came out.

00:11:16.013 --> 00:11:18.641
So for that, you're getting another

00:11:18.641 --> 00:11:20.059
five out of five stars.

00:11:20.059 --> 00:11:21.185
Nico: 10 stars!

00:11:21.185 --> 00:11:24.772
Caroline: 10 stars!
Double fives, you guys.

00:11:24.772 --> 00:11:27.233
You guys, we've done
so many amazing things,

00:11:27.233 --> 00:11:28.609
went to so many beautiful places,

00:11:28.609 --> 00:11:31.404
but I gotta know, do you
have a favorite dare?

00:11:31.404 --> 00:11:32.238
Aj and Nico: Ooh.

00:11:32.238 --> 00:11:33.280
Aj: Oh, I do.

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:34.115
Nico: You do?

00:11:34.115 --> 00:11:35.950
Aj: Yeah, the waterslide in Austria.

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:37.034
Nico: Ooh, fun.

00:11:37.034 --> 00:11:39.245
Caroline: Oh, my gosh, that was amazing.

00:11:39.245 --> 00:11:40.913
That was such a thrill.
Aj: I loved it.

00:11:40.913 --> 00:11:42.164
Nico: I definitely think my favorite

00:11:42.164 --> 00:11:44.208
was the soap-making in Marseille.

00:11:44.208 --> 00:11:47.545
I wasn't expecting the process
to be as hard as it was,

00:11:47.545 --> 00:11:49.255
but everything smelled so good

00:11:49.255 --> 00:11:52.091
and it was so fun to cut
it all up. It was awesome.

00:11:52.091 --> 00:11:53.092
Caroline: I have to say,

00:11:53.092 --> 00:11:55.845
my favorite is absolutely
the Swiss alphorn.

00:11:55.845 --> 00:11:57.805
It was amazing.

00:11:57.805 --> 00:11:59.056
I had such an incredible time.

00:11:59.056 --> 00:12:00.933
It was gonna be the water bikes in Naples,

00:12:00.933 --> 00:12:02.810
but the horn took it away.

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:03.644
Loved it.

00:12:03.644 --> 00:12:04.478
Nico: Yeah, she's gonna move here

00:12:04.478 --> 00:12:05.938
to become a Swiss
alphorn player, for sure.

00:12:05.938 --> 00:12:06.814
Aj: I believe it.

00:12:06.814 --> 00:12:08.524
Caroline: Just leave me
on top of that mountain.

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:11.110
Guys, what a way to end our trip.

00:12:11.110 --> 00:12:12.611
I'm really gonna miss you.

00:12:12.611 --> 00:12:13.988
Nico: We're gonna miss you, too.

00:12:13.988 --> 00:12:15.531
Aj: But hopefully we can do it again soon.

00:12:15.531 --> 00:12:17.366
Caroline: Yes! Cheers to that!

00:12:17.366 --> 00:12:18.492
Nico: Cheers!

00:12:18.492 --> 00:12:20.744
Caroline: Yay, whoops!

00:12:20.744 --> 00:12:21.912
Drink it fast.

